<title>UK: KfW awards mandate for 10-year mark bond.</title>
<headline>KfW awards mandate for 10-year mark bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kreditanstalt Fuer Wiederaufbau (KfW) has appointed Societe Generale and Bayerische Landesbank to lead manage a mark bond, Societe Generale said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The deal will be launched Wednesday afternoon (London time). It will have a 10-year maturity and be a constant maturity rate bond, Societe Generale said.  </p>
<p>The issue will be for 200 million marks, due March 19, 2007. --Reuter London newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
